// A swing is a commitment: presses during one are dropped, not queued.
//
// Four presses, at ticks 0, 5, 19 and 20. **The one at 19 is what pins the
// length**, and the first version of this file was missing it: SWING is 20
// ticks running on 0..19, so testing only tick 20 pins it from one side, and
// shortening RECOVERY to 9 leaves tick 20 free and the trace identical. That
// mutation escaped. With 19 pressed too, a shorter swing accepts it and a
// longer one refuses 20 — either way the trace moves.
//
// No bodies: this is the state machine, and a target would only add contacts.
(
    description: "A press during a swing is dropped; the next one is accepted exactly when recovery ends.",
    setup: (),
    inputs: [],
    attacks: [0, 5, 19, 20],
    budget: (ticks: 45),
    expect: (
        struck: 0,
        hitbox: false,
        enemy_count: 0,
        trace: "a_press_during_a_swing_is_dropped.trace",
    ),
)
